# Component authoring

- One canonical component per function.
- Variants are independent props such as `variant`, `size`, `tone`, `state` and `leadingIcon`.
- Do not infer an icon, role or behavior from visible copy.
- Presentation components receive data and callbacks.
- Interaction state belongs in a colocated hook/controller when it exceeds a small local concern.
- Shared components cannot import features.
- Feature-to-feature access goes through the feature public API.
- No new TSX file above 300 lines.
- No new Sass Module above 500 lines.
- Do not grow a legacy file already above those limits.
- Avoid Effects for values derived from props/state or logic caused by user events.
- Declare lazy imports at module scope and place Suspense around a meaningful user-visible unit.
